--- NOTE on the "old shape" measurement kept in the baseline above ---
The last section of the probe is not a check: it measures what the *old* shape does when two runs name the
same port. One browser is started with a page of its own, a second is started with that port number, and the
second one reports the first browser's page — "it attached to the browser the first run had already opened".
That is the hazard the finding is about, and it is why the port, not only the profile, is per-run now: a
collision here does not fail loudly, it silently drives someone else's browser.

